        "original_id": "0f16f35e-2e4c-5019-aa4c-85ee5e379781",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Erodium, Cymbidium, California macrophylla\n- Taxonomy: Geraniaceae, Orchidaceae, genera, species\n- Places: North Africa, Indomalaya, the Middle East, Australia\n\nFacts:\n- Erodium is a genus of flowering plants in the botanical family Geraniaceae.\n- Erodium includes about 60 species native to North Africa, Indomalaya, the Middle East, and Australia.\n- Cymbidium, or boat orchid, is a genus of 52 evergreen species in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\n- California macrophylla was formerly placed in the genus Erodium and was later moved to its own monotypic genus named California.",
